{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList"},{"type":"text","text":" is a sorted set kept in a skip list (Pugh, 1990): sorted linked lists stacked in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"levels, each level a random sample of the one below, searched from the top level down. Each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element’s tower gains a level with probability 1\/4, so lookup, insertion and removal take"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") expected time with no rebalancing. Its elements are a random-access collection in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ascending order, indexed by rank, with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lowerBound(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"upperBound(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"elements(in:)"},{"type":"text","text":";"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the API matches the sorted sets of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinarySearchTrees"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SkipLists","","var numbers: SkipList = [8, 3, 5, 1, 9]","numbers.insert(4)","numbers.contains(2)     \/\/ false","numbers.lowerBound(5)   \/\/ 3, the index of 5"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The tower heights come from a random number generator given at creation; a seeded one makes every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"list reproducible. The list’s levels are a directed acyclic graph, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList\/layersView-swift.property","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" exposes to Grafluent’s algorithms and drawings as a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(import Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GraphProtocols"},{"text":" module beside this one): a vertex for each element on each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"level of its tower, an edge along each level and an edge down each tower.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/skiplists"]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"SkipLists"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"SkipLists","externalID":"SkipLists","symbolKind":"module"},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists"},"abstract":[{"text":"Skip lists as sorted sets, with their levels as a directed graph.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList"],"title":"Sorted sets","anchor":"Sorted-sets"}],"references":{"doc://SkipLists/documentation/SkipLists/SkipList":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SkipList","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SkipList","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/skiplists\/skiplist","title":"SkipList","identifier":"doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A sorted set kept in a skip list: sorted linked lists stacked in levels, each level a random"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sample of the one below, searched from the top level down (Pugh, 1990)."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://SkipLists/documentation/SkipLists":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Skip lists as sorted sets, with their levels as a directed graph."}],"title":"SkipLists","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/skiplists"},"doc://SkipLists/documentation/SkipLists/SkipList/layersView-swift.property":{"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"layersView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SkipList","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:9SkipLists0A4ListV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">.","kind":"text"},{"text":"LayersView","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:9SkipLists0A4ListVAASHRzrlE10LayersViewV"}],"title":"layersView","role":"symbol","conformance":{"constraints":[{"code":"Element","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"code":"Comparable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}]},"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/skiplists\/skiplist\/layersview-swift.property","abstract":[{"text":"The list’s levels as a directed graph: a vertex for each element on each level of its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tower, an edge from each to the next element on the same level, and an edge from each down","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the same element on the level below. The head is not a vertex.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList\/layersView-swift.property","type":"topic"}}}